7c4c4704400b5f100","file":"preprints/The-Solomon-Yau-least-volume-theorem-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":27,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"3dae357ef5df76e54181300adc67a24e3229bc311d4614d2ea8d1593cd7aa369","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-Solomon-Yau-least-volume-theorem-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:a26ac4471aff99d1111969cb6597a8bfc10906419c8e9b17c4c4704400b5f100","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Solomon-Yau-least-volume-theorem-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L27"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:volume}\nLet \\(m\\ge2\\), let \\(M^m\\) be a closed connected smooth manifold, and let\n\\(F:M\\to S^{m+1}\\) be a smooth minimal immersion into the unit round sphere.\nIf \\(F(M)\\) is not totally geodesic, then\n\\[\n\\Vol\\bigl(M,F^*g_{\\mathrm{round}}\\bigr)\\ge a_m.\n\\]"}
